# Spaghetti Meatballs Teigen

Based on [https://cravingsbychrissyteigen.com/blogs/…](https://cravingsbychrissyteigen.com/blogs/recipes/spaghetti-meatballs) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250806172218/https://cravingsbychrissyteigen.com/blogs/recipes/spaghetti-meatballs))

{ rating="4" image="spaghetti_meatballs_teigen.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### For the Meatballs

(Optional) We have always made this with store-bought meatballs

- [ ] 1 cup fresh [breadcrumbs]{ ing="breadcrumbs" } (processed from 3-4 slices white bread)
- [ ] 1/4 cup [milk]{ ing="milk" }
- [ ] 1 lb [ground beef]{ ing="ground-beef" }
- [ ] 1 lb [ground pork]{ ing="ground-pork" }
- [ ] 1 cup finely shredded [Parmigiano Reggiano cheese]{ ing="parmigiano-reggiano-cheese" }, plus more for garnish
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [minced garlic]{ ing="minced-garlic" }
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [chili flakes]{ ing="chili-flakes" }
- [ ] 2 eggs plus [1 egg yolk]{ ing="1-egg-yolk" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [fine dry breadcrumbs]{ ing="fine-dry-breadcrumbs" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }

### For the Sauce

- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, diced (3 cups)
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [minced garlic]{ ing="minced-garlic" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" }
- [ ] 1 (28-oz) plus 1 (14-oz) cans [crushed tomatoes]{ ing="crushed-tomatoes" }
- [ ] 1 (28-oz) can [tomato sauce]{ ing="tomato-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [chili flakes]{ ing="chili-flakes" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried parsley]{ ing="dried-parsley" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried rosemary]{ ing="dried-rosemary" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 3/4 lb [dried spaghetti]{ ing="dried-spaghetti" }
- [ ] [Finely grated Parmesan]{ ing="finely-grated-parmesan" }, for garnish
- [ ] Fresh [basil]{ ing="basil" } for garnish

## Recipe

### Make the Meatballs (Optional)

1. Combine the [breadcrumbs]{ ing="breadcrumbs" } and [milk]{ ing="milk" } in a large bowl; let the crumbs soak up all the milk. Add the [beef]{ ing="ground-beef" } and [pork]{ ing="ground-pork" } to the bowl along with the [cheese]{ ing="parmigiano-reggiano-cheese" }, [garlic]{ ing="minced-garlic" }, [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, [chili flakes]{ ing="chili-flakes" }, eggs, and [egg yolk]{ ing="1-egg-yolk" }. Gently mix, being careful not to overwork the meat, then form into about 18 golf ball-sized meatballs. Arrange on a large baking sheet and sprinkle very lightly on both sides with the [fine dry breadcrumbs]{ ing="fine-dry-breadcrumbs" } (just a super light dusting). Chill for 1 hour and up to 24 hours (this helps the meatballs keep their shape).
1. Heat the [oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } in a large skillet over medium heat, then add the meatballs (working in batches if you have to) and brown on all sides, 8 minutes total (lower temperature slightly if you need to to avoid any burning). Transfer browned meatballs to a large plate, and carefully drain all but 1/4 cup fat and oil in the skillet. Cover to keep the meatballs warm.

### Make the Sauce

1. Heat the fat and [oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } left over from the meatballs over medium heat. Add the [onions]{ ing="onion" } and cook, stirring, until softened and translucent, 10 minutes. Add the [garlic]{ ing="minced-garlic" } and cook for 1 more minute. Add the [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" } and cook, stirring, until caramelized and absorbed, 2 minutes. Stir in the [crushed tomatoes]{ ing="crushed-tomatoes" }, [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, [chili flakes]{ ing="chili-flakes" }, [thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }, [parsley]{ ing="dried-parsley" }, [rosemary]{ ing="dried-rosemary" }, [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }, and vinegar. Bring to a boil, reduce the heat to low, and simmer until the [sauce]{ ing="tomato-sauce" } thickens, 25 to 30 minutes.
1. Finish and Serve:
1. Gently nestle the meatballs in the [sauce]{ ing="tomato-sauce" }, return to a simmer and cook until the meatballs are fully cooked through and absorb the sauce, 20-25 minutes. Season with [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and pepper to taste.
1. While the meatballs are simmering in the [sauce]{ ing="tomato-sauce" }, cook the pasta al dente according to package directions. Drain, then add to the pot with the meatballs and sauce, or create individual portions. Garnish with [cheese]{ ing="parmigiano-reggiano-cheese" } and [basil]{ ing="basil" }.

## Notes

1. Have not made this with the ‘2 tsp red wine vinegar’
1. Originally 70 oz crushed tomatoes, but modified to 42 crushed + 28 sauce to better balance out the flavors
